      "sequence_position": 12,
      "problem": "The probability distributions of the independent random variables $X$ and $Y$ are given below.\n\n<table align=\"center\">\n\n<tbody><tr>\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$x$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$3$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$f(x)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.5$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.125$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.25$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.125$</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n</th>\n\n<th width=\"5%\"></th>\n\n<th>\n\n<table align=\"center\" cellpadding=\"10\" rules=\"all\">\n\n<tbody><tr> \n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$y$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$1$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$2$</td>\n</tr>\n\n<tr>\n<td width=\"30\" bgcolor=\"#D6EAF8\" align=\"center\">$f(y)$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.4$</td>\n<td align=\"center\">$0.3$</td>\n</tr>\n\n</tbody></table>\n\n<p></p></th>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n\nFind $\\text{E}[XY].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are *independent* random variables, then\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\cdot Y]=\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y]\n$$\n\nThe expected values of $X$ and $Y$ are calculated as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =0\\cdot 0.5+1\\cdot 0.125+2\\cdot 0.25+3\\cdot 0.125=1 \\\\ \\text{E}[Y] & =0\\cdot 0.3+1\\cdot 0.4+2\\cdot 0.3=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $X$ and $Y$ are independent, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[X\\cdot Y]=\\text{E}[X]\\cdot \\text{E}[Y]=1\\cdot 1=1.\n$$",
